SavanXP

A hobby operating system for x86-64, written from scratch, with a desktop in
the spirit of Windows 2000 and XP. This is its system disk, mounted at /.

Getting around
  - The Start menu has the programs; Files opens on your profile.
  - In the Command Prompt, `help` lists every command with examples.
  - `sysinfo` describes this machine, `df` shows this disk's space and
    `fscheck` checks it.
  - Ctrl+Shift+Esc opens Task Manager.

What lives where
  /bin            POSIX programs, the system's and the ones you install
  /lib            shared libraries
  /icons          the icon catalog
  /system         the rest of the system: the native programs (*.sxe), the
                  wallpapers, file associations, cursors, licenses, the
                  default Start menu and samples to try (/system/samples)
  /users/<name>   your profile: your files, with your settings in Settings
  /tmp            scratch space anyone can write to
  /games, /media  data that installed ports add

Your files belong in your profile. Everything outside it is the system's:
changing it takes elevation, and the next system update may replace it.

If this disk cannot be mounted, SavanXP starts its rescue system instead,
which has a README of its own at /rescue/README.

Third-party notices are in /system/licenses.
